fantry Division SSI","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},"CommonsMetadataExtension":{"value":1.2,"source":"extension","hidden":""},"Categories":{"value":"Files with no machine-readable author|Files with no machine-readable source|Media missing infobox template|Vector version available|PD US Army USAIOH|United States Army divisional combat service identification badges|United States Army infantry division combat service identification badges superseded by SVG replacement|4th Infantry Division (United States) heraldry","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"Assessments":{"value":"","source":"commons-categories","hidden":""},"LicenseShortName":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"UsageTerms":{"value":"Public domain","source":"commons-desc-page"},"AttributionRequired":{"value":"false","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Copyrighted":{"value":"False","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"Restrictions":{"value":"","source":"commons-desc-page","hidden":""},"License":{"value":"pd","source":"commons-templates","hidden":""}},"mime":"image/png"}],"revisions":[{"revid":912912778,"parentid":768628654,"timestamp":"2024-08-20T08:30:16Z","slots":{"main":{"contentmodel":"wikitext","contentformat":"text/x-wiki","content":"==SHOULDER SLEEVE INSIGNIA.==\n\n== {{int:filedesc}} ==\n\n* On a light khaki square, each side two inches in width overall and with one angle up, four green ivy leaves arranged per cross issuing from a small open circle (one leaf in each angle of the square and the vertical and horizontal axis each 2 11/32 inches in length). \n\n=== Symbolism: ===\n\n* The four leaves allude to the numerical designation of the Division while the word \"I-VY\" as pronounced, suggests the characters used in the formation of the Roman numeral \"IV.\"\n\n* Ivy leaves are also symbolic of fidelity and tenacity.\n\n=== Background: ===\n\n* The shoulder sleeve insignia was originally approved on October 30, 1918 for the 4th Division without any background specified for the ivy leaf design.\n\n* The design was embroidered on a square olive background (color of the uniform).\n\n* On July 2, 1958, the design was changed to reflect the light khaki color background.\n\n* It was redesignated for the 4th Infantry Division effective August 4, 1943. \n\n== {{int:license-header}} ==\n\n{{PD-USGov-Military-Army-USAIOH}} - US Army Institute Of Heraldry\n\n{{vva|Insignia_USA_Army_4th_Infantry_Division_SSI.svg}}\n\n[[Category:United States Army divisional combat service identification badges|Infantry 004]]\n[[Category:4th Infantry Division (United States) heraldry]]\n[[Category:United States Army infantry division combat service identification badges superseded by SVG replacement]]\n[[Category:Media missing infobox template]]\n[[Category:United States Army divisional combat service identification badges]]"}}}]},{"pageid":3600865,"ns":6,"title":"File:1coscom.jpg","imagerepository":"local","imageinfo":[{"timestamp":"2008-02-23T01:34:24Z","user":"Kwasura","size":30251,"width":238,"height":258,"thumburl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/96/1coscom.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","thumbwidth":443,"thumbheight":480,"thumbattribs":{"src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/96/1coscom.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","decoding":"async","loading":"lazy","width":443,"height":480},"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/96/1coscom.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","descriptionurl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1coscom.jpg","descriptionshorturl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=3600865","sha1":"a0ef6d8ebc444a23490a5b7ef5f379a8fa2e2380","extmetadata":{"DateTime":{"value":"2008-02-23 01:34:24","source":"mediawiki-metadata","hidden":""},"ObjectName":{"value":"1coscom","source":"mediawiki-metadata"},